  infoBubble: {fileID: 175808324}
  titleText: {fileID: 175808321}
  bodyText: {fileID: 175808320}
  nextButton: {fileID: 175808322}
  backButton: {fileID: 175808323}
  pageIndicator: {fileID: 175808319}
  pageTitles:
  - The Designer
  - Let It Shine
  - Mountford's Influence
  pageBodies:
  - 'The Rose Window was designed by Benjamin Mountford, the English architector
    in New Zealand. He supervised the build of the Cathedral and imported the Gothic
    Revival style to Christchurch early buildings, shaping the city''s unique architectural
    character. '
  - 'The famous West Proch, the spire and the pulpit font were built nder Mountfort''s
    supervision, and the building was finally completed in 1904. '
  - Positioned high on the West Wall, Mountfort designed it so the afternoon sun
    would filter through the 4,000 hand-painted glass pieces, illuminating the nave
    in vibrant colours.
